35,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The late-turn pool is hollow. Overtime covers everything. The pilots succeeded, but only because they were small. We cannot scale that success.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The ledger is a trap. The old grant is frozen, and the operating subsidy is gone. We cannot build on empty promises.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The minutes reveal a data deadlock between ferry and rail. The shells hide voids that stop work for weeks. We must avoid both traps.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The ticketing fees exceed our resurfacing budget. The crews are a third below strength. We are committing to costs we cannot sustain.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow! The stopwatch says waiting is the real thief, not the ticket machines! And the pilots worked perfectly! We should trust the data, not the noise!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, your ledger warning is critical. But if the crews are hollow, even funded plans fail. We must prioritize work the existing rosters can actually absorb.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Victoria, you’re right. The money is frozen, but the crews are the real bottleneck. We must pick a plan that doesn’t break the people we have.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, the data deadlock is structural. We must avoid any plan requiring ferry-rail integration. The shell voids are equally dangerous.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I agree. The data deadlock is a trap. But the hollow crews are the immediate danger. We must avoid plans needing extra hands.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, I agree! But my stopwatch says waiting is the real thief. We must fix the connections, not just the machines. Let’s trust the data!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, waiting is a symptom. The cause is the hollow rosters. We must choose a plan that fits the hands we actually have, not the ones we wish for.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
